- **Description:** Given a string, reverse its characters without using extra space.
- **Solution Code:**
  ```c
  void reverse_string(char* str) {
      if (str == NULL || *str == '\0') return;
      
      char* start = str;
      char* end = str + strlen(str) - 1;
      while (start < end) {
          char temp = *start;
          *start = *end;
          *end = temp;
          start++;
          end--;
      }
  }
  ```
- **Algorithm:** Two pointers approach, swapping characters from the beginning and end moving towards the center.

